From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NanoKVM lab <nanokvm@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 14:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] switch-root: clean detached temporary old root after pivot

When switching from a systemd initrd, pivot_root(".", ".") commonly
succeeds.  The old initramfs root is then detached with umount2(MNT_DETACH),
but its ramfs superblock remains referenced by open root directory file
descriptors and can retain every decompressed cpio page as unevictable
memory.  The success path used to assume pivot+umount was sufficient and
skipped the temporary-filesystem cleanup performed by the MS_MOVE fallback.

Remove the detached temporary root contents on the successful pivot path as
well.  rm_rf_children() operates through the root directory fd and stops at
mount boundaries, so the transferred /dev, /proc, /sys, and /run mounts are
not recursively removed.

This is intentionally kept as a small upstreamable systemd fix rather than a
profile service: the switch-root implementation owns the old-root lifetime,
and all callers benefit when DESTROY_OLD_ROOT is requested.

---
 src/shared/switch-root.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/shared/switch-root.c b/src/shared/switch-root.c
--- a/src/shared/switch-root.c
+++ b/src/shared/switch-root.c
@@ -198,11 +198,24 @@
                          * it will stop at mount boundaries */
                         (void) rm_rf_children(TAKE_FD(old_root_fd), 0, &rb); /* takes possession of the dir fd, even on failure */
                 }
-        } else
-                /* NB: we don't bother with emptying the old root superblock here, under the assumption the
-                 * pivot_root() + umount() sufficiently detached from the superblock to the point we don't
-                 * need to empty it anymore */
+        } else {
+                /* pivot_root() + umount() detaches the old root mount from the
+                 * namespace, but does not necessarily empty a ramfs/tmpfs
+                 * superblock.  Open root directory fds (including those held
+                 * by the initrd and surviving processes) can keep every
+                 * decompressed initramfs page unevictable.  Use the same
+                 * fd-based cleanup as the MS_MOVE fallback. */
+                if (istmp > 0) {
+                        struct stat rb;
+
+                        if (fstat(old_root_fd, &rb) >= 0)
+                                (void) rm_rf_children(TAKE_FD(old_root_fd), 0, &rb);
+                        else
+                                log_debug_errno(errno, "Failed to stat old root directory after pivot, ignoring: %m");
+                }
+
                 log_debug("Pivoting root worked.");
+        }
 
         return 0;
 }
